{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{Zar}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S_{affine, Zar} \\to S_{Zar}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh(S_{affine, Zar})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh(S_{Zar})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-alternative-zariski}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1126db69f6a7c7a7bdc910b009ed1159a6bf06f502c5f55bd3e4ffccc9f4c924", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d388a18e2ffef822eddc758298b6841e1404b0ad45a9b14479e2a1c44fcd08a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.  Let <MATH_0002> be a big Zariski\nsite containing <MATH_0003>. The functor <MATH_0004>\nis a special cocontinuous functor. Hence it induces an equivalence\nof topoi from <MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a51efab7771c3a8a34a3b47703204f970571a9d6b2920cb58700fdf7127cef38", "unit_id": "tag:0F1B:statement"}
