{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U/S$", "MATH_0002": "$S_{Zar}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$S_{Zar}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}'(U/S) = \\mathcal{F}(\\Im(U \\to S))$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0009": "$U'/S \\in \\Ob(S_{Zar})$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Im(U' \\to S) = U$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0012": "$S_{Zar}$", "MATH_0013": "$S$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G}'(U) = \\mathcal{G}(U'/S)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0016": "$U = \\bigcup_{i \\in I} U_i$", "MATH_0017": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\{U_j' \\to U'\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0019": "$S_{Zar}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-lemma-what-is-in-it}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-lemma-tautological-same-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:20f26e867448dfe90ee8a22b41ee45b9b5eaf6102e16753188c00e97f1760694", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60670347b5d477813008eafddd31562257441b3e66fc6f2430cf22553e02956f", "source_text": "We will use repeatedly that for any object\n<MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002> the morphism <MATH_0003> is an isomorphism\nonto an open subscheme.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf on <MATH_0005>. Then we define a sheaf\non <MATH_0006> by the rule <MATH_0007>.\nFor the converse, we choose for every open subscheme <MATH_0008> an object\n<MATH_0009> with <MATH_0010>\n(here you have to use Sets, Lemma <REF_0001>).\nGiven a sheaf <MATH_0011> on <MATH_0012> we define a sheaf on <MATH_0013> by setting\n<MATH_0014>. To see that <MATH_0015> is\na sheaf we use that for any open covering <MATH_0016>\nthe covering <MATH_0017>\nis combinatorially equivalent to a covering <MATH_0018>\nin <MATH_0019> by Sets, Lemma <REF_0002>,\nand we use Sites, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nDetails omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba8f400c6d95c4d588b01abfab6ac3c16c3f18b822144aed1e5ce8d34d376f1f", "unit_id": "tag:020X:proof"}
